// app/i18n/featurePages/en.js
//
// The English block for /features and /features/<slug>.
//
// ══ Why English is here at all ═════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// Same reason as the English block behind lib/marketing/featureLabels.js, and
// it is worth restating because it looks like a duplicate and is one:
// scripts/check-translations.mjs works by comparing every language against the
// KEYS OF ENGLISH. A key present in Ukrainian and absent from English is
// reported as "not in English" and fails the run. So English has to exist in
// the catalogue for the other five to be gated at all.
//
// Everything under `featurePage.<slug>.*` is a COPY of app/data/featurePages.js
// and is generated from it. It is pinned: scripts/check-feature-pages.mjs
// asserts every one of these strings is character-identical to the page data,
// and names the ones that are not, so the duplicate cannot rot into a second,
// unproved wording. Editing prose means editing app/data/featurePages.js —
// which the 1043 assertions read — and then this file to match. The check tells
// you exactly which key drifted.
//
// The rest — `featurePage.chrome.*` and `featuresIndex.*` — is NOT a copy.
// It is the page's own furniture and the catalogue is its only home, which is
// why the components call t() for it with no fallback typed into the JSX.
// `featureGroup.*` and `feature.*.limits` are pinned to
// lib/marketing/featureMatrix.js the same way the names and summaries are.

