  "featurePage.quotes.how.3.step": "The client signs it from wherever they are",
  "featurePage.quotes.how.3.body": "They open a link, tick any extras you offered, and sign. What they saw at the moment they signed is recorded with the signature, so a fortnight later there is no argument about what was agreed.",
  "featurePage.quotes.detail.1.label": "One builder, two doors",
  "featurePage.quotes.detail.1.body": "Creating a quote and editing one are the same screen. They were once two, and they taxed differently — one on the gross subtotal, the other after the discount — so the same quote had two totals depending on which screen saved it last.",
  "featurePage.quotes.detail.2.label": "Saved first, sent second",
  "featurePage.quotes.detail.2.body": "A quote is always written down as a draft before anything is emailed. A send that fails leaves you a draft to retry, never a quote marked as sent that nobody received.",
  "featurePage.quotes.detail.3.label": "Your wording is copied onto the document",
  "featurePage.quotes.detail.3.body": "Your terms and your what-happens-next are stored on the quote itself, so changing your defaults in March does not rewrite what you sent in February.",
